Honour llm.api_base, and stop defaulting it to OpenRouter.

Why: upstream comments out api_base in LiteLLM.raw_completion ("TODO: why is this not
working anymore", utils/llm.py:143 at e23d918), so --llm.api_base is ignored and only
LiteLLM's OLLAMA_API_BASE fallback decides where Ollama calls go. The lab needs the
configured endpoint (the cell's LLM tap) to be the one LiteLLM uses, so this passes it.
The OpenRouter default was presumably why the line was commented out: passed through,
it would send every model with no explicit api_base to OpenRouter. An empty default
(None at runtime, like llm.proxy) keeps LiteLLM's own per-provider default instead.
Listed in agents/sheets/hackingbuddygpt.yaml (patches). Applied with git apply at build.

